{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on 5e20a89d: the installed-registers record form.\n\nAccepted as designed at 45546fd5. Build it.\n\n- INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES is an operator setting, recorded in the\n  configuration commit and named in the deployment receipt. Absent, it\n  keeps today's single register. Explicit, it holds 1 to 32 distinct\n  canonical IDs that include REGISTER_SCOPE, within 4,096 bytes, and an\n  invalid value closes creation.\n- A listed register admits only checked child lineages under a root\n  the index already holds. It grants no birth and no authority, and no\n  request, readable scope or index row adds one.\n- Removing a register needs an operator record that names the affected\n  rooms. Nothing evicts a register automatically.\n\nFor hosted Workers, the configuration commit is the Wrangler file.\nEach of apps/room/wrangler.{grow,lending,demo}.jsonc carries the array\nbeside REGISTER_SCOPE once a Worker has more than one register. Say so\nin docs/deploy.md.\n\nOne use follows on the mini. When I next deploy there, with the flush\nfix, I list H3's register beside G3's, so the retired H3 room creates\nchildren again. I record that with the deployment, and its H3 check\nthen covers an Inbox birth, not only status reads.\n\nO4 still runs on its own dedicated Worker. Keeping OAuth's first live\nexposure apart from dap-demo's rooms is worth a separate Worker even\nwith this record in place.\n\nBuilder: please ratify this report by its own ID so 5e20a89d closes.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}